**Issue**: #429
**Date**: 2026-09-24
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Exact-head spec publication survives stale UNSTABLE mergeability
  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Passing checks precede CLEAN for an existing PR
    Given an OPEN non-draft approved spec PR already exists at head H on its expected branch and base
    And all expected, required, and reported checks for H are terminal passing
    And the aggregate mergeability of that PR is UNSTABLE without separate policy-block evidence
    When the same PR and H later report CLEAN on successive fresh observations without changing checks or the branch
    Then publication waits through UNSTABLE without classifying it as pr_merge_blocked
    And publication creates no second PR or changes H
    And it squash-merges exactly once with --match-head-commit H only after fresh passing CLEAN rechecks

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Explicit policy block remains terminal
    Given an OPEN spec PR at unchanged head H has all expected and reported checks passing
    And the fresh PR evidence explicitly reports BLOCKED by non-CI policy
    When publication observes readiness
    Then it reports pr_merge_blocked with actionable PR, head, and blocker evidence
    And it issues no merge or delivery success

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Terminal check failure overrides stale aggregate readiness
    Given the pinned PR head has a terminal failed required or reported check
    When publication observes checks even if aggregate mergeability is UNSTABLE or CLEAN
    Then it reports actionable pr_check_failed evidence for that check and H
    And it issues no merge or delivery success

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario Outline: Changed or disallowed PR identity fails closed
    Given an approved spec PR was pinned to its OPEN non-draft identity, branch, base, and H
    When a fresh observation finds <change>
    Then publication reports actionable identity or readiness failure for that PR and H
    And it issues no merge or delivery success
    Examples:
      | change             |
      | a different head   |
      | a different branch |
      | a different base   |
      | a closed PR        |
      | a draft PR         |

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Incomplete or unknown evidence does not imply success
    Given expected checks are absent or required or reported checks are pending
    Or aggregate mergeability is UNKNOWN
    When publication observes the same PR and H
    Then it does not issue a merge while readiness is unproven
    And it continues observing healthy nonterminal states without an artificial deadline

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Deterministic regression changes only the erroneous classification
    Given a fixture reuses one existing PR at unchanged H with passing checks and UNSTABLE then CLEAN views
    When the focused regression runs before the readiness fix
    Then it reproduces premature pr_merge_blocked without a merge
    When the same fixture runs after the readiness fix
    Then it sees no duplicate PR and exactly one merge guarded by --match-head-commit H
    And genuine policy, failed-check, and identity-drift rejection scenarios still pass
